\tag{fdip}
\title{Gauss's law and charged multiplicities}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{The [gauge transfer operator](fdip-007Y) acts on all spatial
link fields, while its physical trace uses gauge-invariant states.
Temporal gauge explains the residual symmetry behind this
constraint. With external charges, invariance applies to the link
field together with its charge factors; it does not select a whole
isotypic component of the link space.}

\p{The neutral projector is normalized averaging. Charged invariant
tensors instead identify with a space of intertwiners. A single
permutation-group link distinguishes a four-dimensional isotypic
component from a one-dimensional charged space. A two-by-two sign
lattice then counts neutral states by its gauge orbits. All graphs
and time intervals here are finite.}

